        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "50b88a35-b358-5745-8e54-615fbff3f70f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Dahlia, Aruncus, Butea monosperma, Coreopsis, Toxicodendron vernicifluum, Rhus verniciflua\n- Concepts: genera, herbaceous perennial plants, tuberous plants, Rosaceae, butein, antioxidative effects, aldose reductase inhibition, advanced glycation endproducts inhibition\n\nFacts:\n- Dahlia is a genus of bushy, tuberous, herbaceous perennial plants native to Mexico.\n- Aruncus is a genus of clump-forming herbaceous perennial plants in the family Rosaceae.\n- Toxicodendron vernicifluum, formerly called Rhus verniciflua, contains butein.\n- Dahlia, Butea monosperma, and Coreopsis contain butein.\n- Butein has antioxidative effects.\n- Butein has aldose reductase inhibitory effects.\n- Butein has advanced glycation endproducts inhibitory effects.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
